<%# The composer is the one part of the page that is pure behaviour: which key
    sends, where the button sits, what a turn in flight does to both. It is
    kept as a partial so the markup the JavaScript addresses has a place of
    its own — and a name in a test.

    `x-ref="form"` is what the keydown handler submits through. Without it the
    handler throws on `undefined.requestSubmit()` and Enter stops sending. -%>
<form class="composer"
      x-ref="form"
      data-draft="<%= h(session_id) %>"
      hx-post="/s/<%= h(session_id) %>/turn<%= h(token_query) %>"
      hx-target="#thread"
      hx-swap="beforeend"
      x-data="composer">
  <%# A paragraph quoted from an answer rides above the field rather than in
      it: it is carried into the turn as context, and the field stays the place
      the reader types. One chip per paragraph, droppable before sending, so a
      wrong quote costs a click instead of a rewrite. Stitching the quote into
      the message is the composer's job (app.js): the form this element posts
      carries the typed text, and the quote is added on the way out. -%>
  <div class="composer-quotes" x-show="quotes.length" x-cloak>
    <template x-for="quote in quotes" :key="quote.id">
      <div class="composer-quote">
        <div class="quote-body">
          <span class="quote-kind" x-show="quote.kind" x-text="quote.kind"></span>
          <span class="quote-text" x-text="quote.preview"></span>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="quote-remove"
                x-on:click="unquote(quote.id)"
                aria-label="Hapus kutipan" title="Hapus kutipan"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12"
                width="11" height="11" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"
                stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3.2 3.2l5.6 5.6M8.8 3.2 3.2 8.8"/></svg></button>
      </div>
    </template>
  </div>
  <%# The chips are a visual addition, so the count is spoken here instead —
      outside the block that hides itself, because a live region inside a
      `display: none` parent announces nothing. -%>
  <span class="sr-only" aria-live="polite" x-text="quoteStatus"></span>
  <%# The field and its button are one line, so the button sits at the end of
      the text rather than under it: a row is what keeps the two in the same
      band as the field grows. -%>
  <div class="composer-row">
    <textarea x-ref="input"
              x-model="text"
              name="message"
              rows="1"
              aria-label="Pesan"
              placeholder="Tulis pesan… Enter mengirim, Shift+Enter baris baru"
              x-on:keydown="keydown($event)"></textarea>
    <div class="composer-actions">
      <%# Two buttons, and only while a turn is running: a phone has no Enter
          that sends, so during a turn the reader has to be able to do both
          things they might mean — hand the running turn another instruction,
          or stop it. One button that turned into the other meant steering was
          simply unavailable on a phone, which is exactly where the software
          keyboard's Enter key can only make a new line.

          While the session is free the second button is not in the page at
          all: there is nothing to stop, and a control that does nothing is
          worse than one that is absent.

          Both are drawn as an icon. Two words beside the field were chrome
          for the two things every prompt does, and on a phone they took the
          width the field itself needs. The word is not lost: it is in
          `title` and in `aria-label`, so the button is still named to a
          screen reader and still explains itself under a mouse. -%>
      <button type="button"
              class="btn primary"
              x-on:click="send()"
              x-bind:disabled="!text.trim() || compacting"
              aria-label="Kirim"
              x-bind:title="compacting ? 'Menunggu compaction selesai' : (busy ? 'Kirim sebagai arahan ke turn yang berjalan' : 'Kirim')"
              ><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="15" height="15" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M11.47 2.47a.75.75 0 0 1 1.06 0l7.5 7.5a.75.75 0 1 1-1.06 1.06l-6.22-6.22V21a.75.75 0 0 1-1.5 0V4.81l-6.22 6.22a.75.75 0 1 1-1.06-1.06l7.5-7.5Z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg></button>
      <button type="button"
              class="btn composer-stop"
              x-show="busy"
              x-bind:disabled="stopping"
              x-bind:aria-busy="stopping"
              x-on:click="stop()"
              x-bind:aria-label="stopLabel"
              x-bind:title="stopLabel"
              ><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="15" height="15" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M4.5 7.5a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h9a3 3 0 0 1 3 3v9a3 3 0 0 1-3 3h-9a3 3 0 0 1-3-3v-9Z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg></button>
    </div>
  </div>
</form>
